# render_shrink.cxc -- master script. Run it with:
#
#     chimerax --offscreen --script render_shrink.cxc
#
# --offscreen renders without a display, which is what you want on a cluster
# node. Drop it to watch the shot build in a window.
#
# Everything it opens is written by prep_shrink.py, so run that first:
#
#     python3 prep_shrink.py --design your_design.cif --receptor input/6w74.pdb
#
# Paths below are relative to the working directory, not to this file. Run
# from the repository root.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# models, palette and choreography
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 00_open.cxc carries the open order and the `coordset true` flags; both are
# generated because the numbering depends on whether a full-length model
# exists. generated.cxc carries the palette, the named selections, the
# playback aliases with frame counts baked in, and the counter text with the
# real measured numbers.
open output/00_open.cxc
open output/generated.cxc
open 00_setup.cxc

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# output
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
windowsize 1920 1080

# supersample 3 is 9x the pixels per frame and the single biggest quality
# lever here. Drop it to 1 while blocking timing, put it back for the final
# pass. Budget roughly 1-5 s/frame at 1080p supersample 3, so about half an
# hour for the ~315 frames this shot runs to.
movie record supersample 3 format png

open 10_shots.cxc

movie encode output/e3_shrink.mp4 framerate 30 quality high
exit

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# compositing over the animated sequence instead of cutting to it
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# mp4 cannot carry an alpha channel. To get the molecular shot on a
# transparent background so it can sit over the cartoon frames, replace the
# three commands above with:
#
#   set bgColor none
#   movie record supersample 3 format png directory output/png transparentBackground true
#   open 10_shots.cxc
#   movie stop
#
# which leaves a numbered PNG sequence in output/png/ for the editor.
#
# Note that `lighting soft` shadows land on the molecule itself, not on a
# ground plane, so they survive the transparent background intact.
